"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116346","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116346","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116346.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116346.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113833\r\n\r\nPreviously GpuParticlesAttractorFieldVector3D would only apply correctly to GpuParticles3D that were created on the same frame or later than the GpuParticlesAttractorVectorField3D. See issue for more details and a minimal reproduction.\r\n\r\nIt looks like the intention of the logic here was to update the textures for the particles when they are first created (`uniform_set_valid == false`), or when the set of textures overlapping with the particles has changed (`different == true`). However, it seems like the logic for the latter case was incomplete, and that path was never being taken.\r\n\r\nI confirmed that the minimal reproduction is fixed by these changes.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116346/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116346/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}